{
  "description": "Integrate LakeSail Sail as a supported BenchBox platform for high-performance\nSpark-compatible SQL and DataFrame benchmarking.\n\nLakeSail Sail is a Rust-based, drop-in replacement for Apache Spark that delivers\nsignificant performance improvements while maintaining full Spark SQL and DataFrame\nAPI compatibility. Key characteristics:\n\n- **4x faster execution** with 94% lower hardware costs vs Apache Spark (TPC-H SF100)\n- **Zero rewrite migration**: Uses standard PySpark client via Spark Connect protocol\n- **Dual execution modes**: Multi-threaded single-host or distributed cluster\n- **Modern architecture**: Built on DataFusion with Rust workers\n- **Active development**: Supports Spark 3.5 and 4.0, with roadmap for streaming\n\nThis is a strategic platform addition because:\n1. Growing interest in Spark alternatives with better performance/cost ratios\n2. Direct comparison with existing Spark adapter validates performance claims\n3. DataFrame API support enables benchbox dataframe mode (-df suffix)\n4. Open-source with commercial support model fits enterprise evaluation needs\n\nTechnical approach:\n- Leverage existing PySpark client (Sail implements Spark Connect server)\n- Can potentially reuse significant code from spark.py/pyspark adapters\n- SQLGlot 'spark' dialect for query translation\n- Support both local (single-node) and distributed deployment modes\n\nReference implementations:\n- benchbox/platforms/spark.py (SQL-based Spark)\n- benchbox/platforms/pyspark/sql_adapter.py (PySpark SQL)\n- benchbox/platforms/dataframe/pyspark_df.py (PySpark DataFrame)",
